{"id": "16222", "revid": "1423298", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=16222", "title": "Jefferson Parish", "text": "Jefferson Parish is in Louisiana, in the Greater New Orleans region. The parish seat is Gretna, located on the Westbank.\nRegions.\nLocations within Jefferson Parish, like all of the New Orleans metropolitan area, can be conveniently thought of in terms of their relation to the Mississippi River. Locals frequently divide the parish into the Eastbank (on the north-ish side) and the Westbank (on the south-ish side of the river).\nUnderstand.\nMost of the population of Jefferson Parish are in the communities adjacent to New Orleans and along the Mississippi River. The Parish also includes smaller communities along the bayous and bays stretching south to the Gulf of Mexico.\nGet in.\nGreater New Orleans' main airport, Armstrong International, is in Kenner.\nInterstate 10 runs through the Eastbank.\nU.S. Highway 90 runs through the Westbank; for much of the distance it has a limited-access elevated freeway down the center, the \"Westbank Expressway\"."}
{"id": "16224", "revid": "2236161", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=16224", "title": "Jeffersontown", "text": "Jeffersontown is a town located in the Kentucky Derby Region. It is the second largest city in Jefferson County and is part of Louisville Metro.\nGet in.\nJeffersontown is easily reached by exiting I-64 at Exit 15 (Hurstbourne Pkwy) or Exit 17 (Blankenbaker Pkwy). It can also be reached by taking I-265 to Exit 19 (Billtown Rd) or Exit 23 (Taylorsville Rd, KY 155).\nA more scenic route into the town is to travel down Taylorsville Road (KY 155) east about 5 miles from the Watterson Expressway (I-264 - Exit 17 A)."}
